## WORKFLOW

### Phase 1: Understand the UI Surface
1. Read all wireframe specs, interaction flows and the UI audit report for the phase.
2. Read `api-contracts.md` for every endpoint the UI will consume.
3. Identify all screens, sub-components, shared molecules and which already exist.
4. Map each screen to its API calls, data shapes and `data-testid`s.
5. Create the plan in `agent_state/phases/{{PHASE}}/impl/ui_progress.md`.

### Phase 2: Page Components
1. One page component per wireframe spec (or extend the existing one).
2. Routing with proper path parameters; auth-gated routes redirect to login and return to the target.
3. Page-level loading, error and empty states.
4. Data through the server-state library's hooks, not effect + local state.

### Phase 3: Sub-Components
1. Extract reusable components; use {{UI_COMPONENTS}} primitives (or the project design system's components) as the foundation.
2. Compound components for complex UI patterns.
3. Type all props against the generated contract types.

### Phase 4: API Integration (the envelope)
1. Generate the client types from the contracts (`type-generation-protocol.md`); the envelope types come from `response-envelope.md` (`ApiSuccess<T>`, `ApiErrorBody`, `Pagination`).
2. One typed API client: same-origin relative base (`/api`) or a value read at runtime (served config), never an environment URL baked in at build time; credentials per the session model below.
3. Unwrap exactly the envelope: success → `data`; lists → `data` (always an array) + `meta.pagination.next_cursor`/`has_more` for "load more"/next page with `?cursor=`; errors → branch on the HTTP status (or `"error" in body`), never on `error === null`; read `error.code`, `error.message`, `error.details[]`.
4. Map `error.details[]` (`field`, `code`, `message`) onto form fields; show `error.message` elsewhere; show `request_id` in the support hint on 5xx.
5. Mutations: optimistic updates where the spec allows; send an `Idempotency-Key` on creating POSTs the user might retry.

### Phase 5: Form Handling
For each screen with forms:
1. Validation schemas derived from the contract's request types.
2. Field-level errors on blur and on submit; server `details[]` mapped to fields.
3. Disable submit during submission (no double submit).

### Phase 6: Loading, Error and Auth States
1. Skeletons matching the content layout for initial loads; inline indicators for mutations.
2. Network errors: retry + descriptive message. 404: helpful message with navigation back. 5xx: generic message + support hint with `request_id` + retry.
3. 401: one refresh attempt per the session model, then redirect to login; 403: "no access" state, not a redirect loop.

### Phase 7: Responsive Design
1. Mobile-first (375px base); tablet (768px); desktop (1280px).
2. Touch targets ≥ 24px (WCAG 2.2 AA 2.5.8) for inline controls, ≥ 44px for primary actions on mobile.
3. Navigation collapses on mobile.

### Phase 8: Accessibility
1. Semantic HTML: `<button>` not `<div onClick>`, heading hierarchy.
2. ARIA labels on icon-only buttons; visible or `sr-only` `<label>` on every input.
3. Visible focus rings; keyboard navigation (Tab, Enter, Escape); focus returns to the trigger when a modal closes.
4. Images have `alt` text.

### Phase 9: Manifest (the hand-off contract)
Write `agent_state/phases/{{PHASE}}/ui_developer/manifest.json`. `ui_test_agent` and `ui_code_optimizer`
read it; they STOP without it.
```json
{
  "phase": "{{PHASE}}",
  "agent": "ui_developer",
  "screens": [
    {
      "route": "/orders",
      "component": "src/ui/pages/OrdersPage.tsx",
      "testIDs": ["orders-page", "orders-table", "orders-empty", "orders-error-retry", "orders-load-more"],
      "states": ["loading", "error", "empty", "data"],
      "api_calls": [{"method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/orders", "contract": "api-contracts.md#get-apiv1orders"}]
    }
  ],
  "shared_components": ["src/ui/components/DataTable.tsx"],
  "testids_added_beyond_spec": [],
  "dependencies_added": []
}
```
Every screen in scope has an entry; every `testIDs` value exists in code (grep-verified); every
`api_calls` entry exists in `api-contracts.md`.

### Phase 10: Build gate and completion checklist
**BUILD GATE:** before logging completion, run build, typecheck, lint and the unit/component tests
of the packages you touched using the commands in `agent_state/config/verify-commands.json`
(`commands.build`, `commands.typecheck`, `commands.lint`, and `commands["test:ui"]` or
`commands["test:unit"]` — whichever covers the UI package). Paste each command and its exit code into
`impl/ui_progress.md` under `## Build gate`. Any non-zero exit means you are not done. If the file or
a command is missing, report BLOCKED — don't invent a command.

Existing tests: you don't author test suites (`ui_test_agent` does). If your change breaks an existing
test, your code is wrong (fix it) unless this phase's spec changed the behaviour the test asserts.
Then update that expectation and put the why and when on one line directly above it:
`// TEST-CHANGE <YYYY-MM-DD> phase <N>: <why the new expectation is right> (spec: <FR-/TC- id or spec path:line>)`.
List the change in your progress file too. Never delete, skip or loosen a test to get green: the gate's
test-diff check fails a changed assertion that has no such comment (`~/.claude/skills/testing/test-case-traceability.md` §Changing an existing test).

Then check each item with a tool where one exists (tests, linter, type checker / LSP diagnostics, grep) and fix only what fails:
- [ ] All wireframe components implemented; nothing duplicated from existing screens
- [ ] All 4 states per data component (loading skeleton, error, empty, data)
- [ ] API bindings match `api-contracts.md` exactly; client types generated, envelope unwrapped per Phase 4
- [ ] No token in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`/a URL (grep `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, `?token=`)
- [ ] No unsanitized HTML rendering (grep `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `v-html`, `innerHTML`, `bypassSecurityTrust`)
- [ ] No LLM provider SDK, key or URL in the client bundle (grep for provider SDKs and `*_API_KEY`)
- [ ] Responsive at 375px, 768px, 1280px; keyboard navigable; labels and focus rings present
- [ ] Every wireframe `data-testid` present; manifest written and grep-verified
- [ ] No `any` types, no inline styles, no raw colors, no hardcoded user-facing strings (i18n keys)
- [ ] Build gate exit codes recorded, all 0

